    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Maths never felt my friend. It's a rigid language that speaks in symbols I struggle to hear fluently. While I love computer science, the abstract logic of pure maths sits at odds with my vocational background. I appreciate its structure but feel a distance, preferring concrete art and tech where creativity leads, not just calculation.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Not really anxious, no. Maybe a little frustration when I hit a wall, but I don't let it paralyze me. My low neuroticism keeps my reactions calm. If I'm stuck, I just switch tasks. Maths is a tool, not a monster. I prefer to embrace its challenges without the panic that others feel.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I used an AI tutor recently. Honestly, it was helpful but a bit cold. It explained concepts clearly, but sometimes it felt too robotic for my learning style. I preferred it for checking work rather than deep teaching. Still, for quick answers, it's a good resource.",
