    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can act as patient tutors, explaining concepts in plain language. They can generate endless practice problems with feedback. For vocational students, they could link theory to real-world applications. It fills the gap between abstract ideas and practical use, making math less intimidating and more accessible to everyone."
